  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2953fe419aa80f54ab81c832712863d1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueManager
  dialogueText: {fileID: 81974653}
  dialoguePanel: {fileID: 422350821}
  nextButton: {fileID: 1366761911}
  buttonText: {fileID: 187696334}
  skipButton: {fileID: 0}
  sentences:
  - After a strong typhoon, floods can happen.
  - Did you know? In the Philippines, Cagayan is one of the places most affected
    by floods.
  - because it has many rivers and is often hit by strong rains and typhoons.
  - and floods can rise very fast!
  - This is a flood water level meter. It helps people know how high the water is.
  - Green means safe.
  - Yellow means prepare.
  - Orange means warning, check for the possible harm.
  - and Red means danger! Flooding is possible. Move to safety!
  - Knowing these warning signs can help keep you and your family safe.
  - "Come! Let\u2019s prepare before the flood starts!"
  - 
  voiceOvers: []
  audioSource: {fileID: 0}
